            title: 'Tonk',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tonk (or Tunk) is a fast-paced matching card game popular in the USA. It combines features of Rummy and 'Knock' games (like Gin). Players aim to form spreads (books/runs) or 'Drop' (knock) with a low point count.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Popularized in the mid-20th century, particularly in African American communities and jazz culture.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card. Face=10, A=1, Num=Value.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards, chips',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal 5 (or 7) cards to each.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
